    "project_template_level_name": "aif-y2-natural-language-processing-lesson10-2026 + template",
    "long_instructions": "`predict` returns a list of tokens, like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[\"students\", \"the\", \"cafeteria\", \"will\", \"be\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo print it as a single string, you need to turn the list back into a single string. The `detokenize` function should do just that.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Complete the `detokenize` function.\r\n  - Join the tokens in `tokens` into a single string, with a space between each token.\r\n  - Return the resulting string.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\n`\" \".join` combines a list of strings into one string, with a space between each item.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\" \".join([\"students\", \"the\", \"cafeteria\", \"will\", \"be\"]) # \"students the cafeteria will be\"\r\n```",
